    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d621">

                <pb facs="0611" n="541" xml:id="pg541"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.30/20: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Weddell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-07-05T23:00:00-04:00">July 5, 1934—11
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 6—1:02 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>98. For Secretary and Under Secretary. Referring to Department’s No. 55, June 21,
                    7 p.m. Minister of Foreign Affairs informed me last night that offer contained
                    therein was accepted in principle but not as a mission but as a simple contract
                    between the Argentine Government and officers selected and that Argentine
                    Ambassador had been telegraphically advised to this effect. Foregoing has been
                    confirmed at Navy Department today by Commander Strother.<anchor n="19"
                        xml:id="d621-f1"/> Argentine Government most desirous of avoiding premature
                    publicity and I suggest that their wish be made known to Navy authorities.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Weddell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d621-f1" n="19" xml:id="d621-f1-content">
                <p>Commander Edmund W. Strother, Naval Attaché.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
